{"seconds": 53.6, "exit": 0, "final": "Excellent! After Bd6 Qxd6 Rxd6, White has won the queen for a bishop (+9 material advantage).\n\nSo the best move is **Bd6**, and the main line is:\n- 1. Bd6 (threatens the queen and rook)\n- If 1...Rxe3 2. Bxc7 winning the queen\n- If 1...Qxd6 2. Rxd6 winning the queen\n- If 1...Re8 (or other queen moves) 2. Bxe5 winning the rook\n\nThis is a **fork** - the bishop simultaneously attacks both the queen on c7 and the rook on e5.\n\n---\n\n**Best move:** Bd6\n\n**Main line:** Bd6 Rxe3 Bxc7 Rxc7 Qxc4\n\n**Motif:** fork\n\n**Explanation:**\nYour bishop on a3 has a devastating fork: move it to d6 and it attacks both Black's queen on c7 and undefended rook on e5 simultaneously. Black must lose material either way\u2014if the rook takes your pawn, you capture the queen with Bxc7; if the queen recaptures your bishop, you play Rxd6 winning it back. This pattern (attacking two pieces at once, forcing material loss) appears throughout chess. Spot the square where one piece can hit two enemy pieces\u2014that's often the killer move.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Bd6\", \"line\": [\"Bd6\", \"Rxe3\", \"Bxc7\", \"Rxc7\", \"Qxc4\", \"Qxc4\"], \"motifs\": [\"fork\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "2r3k1/p1q2ppp/1p3n2/4r3/Q1p5/B3P3/P4PPP/1R1R2K1 w - - 0 21"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "2r3k1/p1q2ppp/1p3n2/4r3/Q1p5/B3P3/P4PPP/1R1R2K1 w - - 0 21"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-forcing_lines", "args": {"fen": "2r3k1/p1q2ppp/1p3n2/4r3/Q1p5/B3P3/P4PPP/1R1R2K1 w - - 0 21"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "2r3k1/p1q2ppp/1p3n2/4r3/Q1p5/B3P3/P4PPP/1R1R2K1 w - - 0 21"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "2r3k1/p1q2ppp/1p3n2/4r3/Q1p5/B3P3/P4PPP/1R1R2K1 w - - 0 21", "move": "Qe8+"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "2r3k1/p1q2ppp/1p3n2/4r3/Q1p5/B3P3/P4PPP/1R1R2K1 w - - 0 21", "move": "Qd7"}}, {"tool"